  "lineage": "Brazilian coco northeastern-Brazilian song-and-dance tradition of Pernambuco, Paraíba, and Alagoas, descended from the African-Brazilian colonial-period rural-work-song tradition (coco was originally a coconut-husking work-song with stamping-rhythm accompaniment). Performance: lead singer with chorus response, hand-clapping or ganzá-shaker rhythm, occasional pandeiro frame-drum. Repertoire spans rural-worker thematic content, coastal-fishing themes, and romantic-couplet improvisation. Genre revival under Nação Zumbi and Chico Science in 1990s integrated coco with rock-and-electronic-production.",
